**6 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**2 [[Bun Bun Black]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is the trickiest of the stages. You don't want to be overly aggressive at the beginning since loads of strong enemies will spawn once the base is hit,  but if you are too cautious the peons will overrun you or force a response that accidentally pushes to the base. Try your best to kill the enemies with slow-moving cats or optionally let your units be killed by the weaker peons after dealing with the more dangerous ones so stalling is easier.

Spam 3-4 meatshields to stall out at the beginning and slow the advance of the enemy waves after hitting the base. Once you have enough money, go all out with your area attack midrangers ([[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]]) and backliners ([[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]]) to handle the enemies, as money isn't a huge issue after the base is hit. By this point, you should also have some [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]] and unit [[True Form]]s, as they will make beating and farming the stage far easier.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: An excellent pick thanks to its spammability, decent range, high dps, and high damage against floating when stacked. It also attacks rapidly which can hold the enemies at bay.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Annihilates most of the enemies with ease due to having Massive damage against Dark enemies and rapid attacks.
*[[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]]: Can be used to relieve some pressure off the frontline if you are not confident in your meatshielding or ability to melt the enemies before they push too far.
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]: Cripples the Bun Bun Blacks, allowing you to focus on the other threats in the stage.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Disables every single enemy in the stage. Essentially a free win here if you use this unit.

